# API3 - Broken Object Property Level Authorisation (Mass Assignment)
# NOT DETECTABLE at the web tier. No rule is provided.
#
# Tested 19 Sep 2026: 29 PUT requests to /identity/api/v2/user/email with
# role and isAdmin injected into the request body. All 29 produced access log
# entries identical in path, method, status and response size.
#
# The injected fields exist only in the request body, which nginx does not
# log. crapi-identity's configured log level records no request detail.
# No field at either tier distinguishes this attack from any other rejected
# request to the same endpoint.
#
# Detection would require application-tier logging of request properties,
# or $request_body in the nginx log_format, which carries a privacy cost.
